find ${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$ as a function of ${f}^{-1}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y=3{x}^{3}+9x,$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=3{y}^{3}+9y\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={f}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(3{y}^{3}+9y) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =9{y}^{2}+9 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{9{y}^{2}+9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${f}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={f}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{f}^{-1}(x)] & =\\frac{1}{9{({f}^{-1}(x))}^{2}+9} \\\\ {({f}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{9{({f}^{-1}(x))}^{2}+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-73064/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c0b7d95-c699-5762-aa44-449712f035c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73064"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-110045/selection/03774d4a207e796bbbf46ba013158cf58940b7028f62b7c87d9a46c8786465c1" :answer/id #uuid "d0439fb8-285d-58ae-8d21-45d07193ac91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}+6({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}+16({h}^{-1}(x))}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110045/selection/424cb6bcb0962d0a571d955b2e801a8bb1d994882c3052b3089b6f874333b43a" :answer/id #uuid "8366b443-8880-5877-9f6f-e1644a1546f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10({h}^{-1}(x))^{4}+3({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}-8({h}^{-1}(x))}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110045/selection/9358ccf374d8971ad5fecf1ed6d350b8a16dc79a2afaff7b5a876195fc09205c" :answer/id #uuid "bd39c4f9-b65d-53c9-9fb5-2875d85a51f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}-3({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}-6({h}^{-1}(x))}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110045/selection/a519d93d9e0b290e6ce533e990ab88471a3dd232adc8988306a935dafc332dc0" :answer/id #uuid "1bd2fd1e-80b3-5882-b5ff-8cd62010899c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}+6({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}-16({h}^{-1}(x))}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110045/selection/43eab9f3778110003d778cacf5ef65b8c607070b9ec2c1e6f3187e2e9fb6ed94" :answer/id #uuid "5c817d1d-b88c-52d3-a3f6-c59692c44f1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}-2({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}-16({h}^{-1}(x))}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110045/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "61bf5b6d-a7af-5039-b409-0dc025a78e74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110045/selection/a519d93d9e0b290e6ce533e990ab88471a3dd232adc8988306a935dafc332dc0" :answer-field/choices ["q-110045/selection/03774d4a207e796bbbf46ba013158cf58940b7028f62b7c87d9a46c8786465c1" "q-110045/selection/424cb6bcb0962d0a571d955b2e801a8bb1d994882c3052b3089b6f874333b43a" "q-110045/selection/9358ccf374d8971ad5fecf1ed6d350b8a16dc79a2afaff7b5a876195fc09205c" "q-110045/selection/a519d93d9e0b290e6ce533e990ab88471a3dd232adc8988306a935dafc332dc0" "q-110045/selection/43eab9f3778110003d778cacf5ef65b8c607070b9ec2c1e6f3187e2e9fb6ed94"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110045" :question/id #uuid "0e0661d3-5ec7-5492-854f-de5461f920f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-110045" :question/problem "If $h(x)=5{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}-10,$ find ${({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$ as a function of ${h}^{-1}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y=5{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}-10,$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=5{y}^{4}+2{y}^{3}-8{y}^{2}-10\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={h}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(5{y}^{4}+2{y}^{3}-8{y}^{2}-10) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =20{y}^{3}+6{y}^{2}-16y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{20{y}^{3}+6{y}^{2}-16y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${h}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={h}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{h}^{-1}(x)] & =\\frac{1}{20({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}+6({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}-16({h}^{-1}(x))} \\\\ {({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{20({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}+6({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}-16({h}^{-1}(x))}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-110045/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c0b7d95-c699-5762-aa44-449712f035c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110045"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-110046/selection/7bba625a3bdd70ebfa8eda3c3238c38a0f163490196fe2071456914be7907580" :answer/id #uuid "a33dc6be-3dfc-5603-8c60-0517320e7874" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{24({h}^{-1}(x))^{5}+16({h}^{-1}(x))^{4}-8({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110046/selection/4bd11a6b751410daf489ff633c5c2e91a04e9cf5fb72f5e8232f9ade49dc923f" :answer/id #uuid "b52ace05-6a2b-5a36-9673-0f75b5d47e2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{48({h}^{-1}(x))^{5}+16({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}+9({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110046/selection/ec7f000ef5f3c376a8021416badb5e7d1a2f61dd3ca30c3bef0f398179bfd67d" :answer/id #uuid "934008cb-5791-5bf3-bb2c-c0081c588f51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{48({h}^{-1}(x))^{4}-16({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}+9({h}^{-1}(x))}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110046/selection/1a41f34d6499c7317fe74166442550bb0e5cdb8415a5eaa64fb60746723f943c" :answer/id #uuid "7d5e96b4-4200-59ee-bd46-a598d9793898" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{48({h}^{-1}(x))^{5}+16({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}-3({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110046/selection/2002317bb5003b0ed931dded1d1cb37a3941e782045a43989d4325629f8940eb" :answer/id #uuid "24439e3f-7b88-576c-b203-a58131ddfeae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8({h}^{-1}(x))^{5}+8({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}+9({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110046/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8dd08776-584c-5ba5-854e-c883f8e400dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110046/selection/4bd11a6b751410daf489ff633c5c2e91a04e9cf5fb72f5e8232f9ade49dc923f" :answer-field/choices ["q-110046/selection/7bba625a3bdd70ebfa8eda3c3238c38a0f163490196fe2071456914be7907580" "q-110046/selection/4bd11a6b751410daf489ff633c5c2e91a04e9cf5fb72f5e8232f9ade49dc923f" "q-110046/selection/ec7f000ef5f3c376a8021416badb5e7d1a2f61dd3ca30c3bef0f398179bfd67d" "q-110046/selection/1a41f34d6499c7317fe74166442550bb0e5cdb8415a5eaa64fb60746723f943c" "q-110046/selection/2002317bb5003b0ed931dded1d1cb37a3941e782045a43989d4325629f8940eb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110046" :question/id #uuid "ca982668-02f8-564e-94b7-165ec7fe8181" :question/math-academy-id "q-110046" :question/problem "If $h(x)=8{x}^{6}+4{x}^{4}+3{x}^{3}-12,$ find ${({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$ as a function of ${h}^{-1}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y=8{x}^{6}+4{x}^{4}+3{x}^{3}-12,$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=8{y}^{6}+4{y}^{4}+3{y}^{3}-12\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={h}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(8{y}^{6}+4{y}^{4}+3{y}^{3}-12) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =48{y}^{5}+16{y}^{3}+9{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{48{y}^{5}+16{y}^{3}+9{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${h}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={h}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{h}^{-1}(x)] & =\\frac{1}{48({h}^{-1}(x))^{5}+16({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}+9({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}} \\\\ {({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{48({h}^{-1}(x))^{5}+16({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}+9({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-110046/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c0b7d95-c699-5762-aa44-449712f035c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110046"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-110048/selection/a051bba0359350686ef4a655a83e94374b6c44a99c23471f5d547a5f12d18722" :answer/id #uuid "a9210eff-9d8c-5308-b628-21c58fedd8ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{cos}^{3}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{3})}{12{[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110048/selection/7375110419d56f674ffdf8fc8c13e0a203f5131a6ebb34c02508c9f6e3dca36e" :answer/id #uuid "7cffd6a6-1759-5f65-a273-3748379d0adb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{csc}^{3}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{3})\\operatorname{sec}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{3})}{12{[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110048/selection/1e1246969018f83ac88efee1a37d262b6f99142c4b4f712c8348e97e14a43105" :answer/id #uuid "d5c52730-54de-5e38-a389-3e120f4c45a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{{cos}^{3}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{3})\\operatorname{sec}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{3})}{6{[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110048/selection/6413bed428971db3ca33a36b959ff6403755f399a59ccde28d247a491228db32" :answer/id #uuid "a0184b72-f861-5763-a3cd-ce6af6adea12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{sec}^{3}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{3})\\operatorname{csc}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{3})}{6{[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110048/selection/b164d22226fc6e1c22c5fbf86a9eb47d04aed7cd22395189e7cdb0ed5538864c" :answer/id #uuid "f4ba0127-5eee-5f95-9504-e984c978dbdf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{3})\\operatorname{sec}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{3})}{3{[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110048/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "446e8a1e-c1da-59e2-907e-e7c32653a8fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110048/selection/7375110419d56f674ffdf8fc8c13e0a203f5131a6ebb34c02508c9f6e3dca36e" :answer-field/choices ["q-110048/selection/a051bba0359350686ef4a655a83e94374b6c44a99c23471f5d547a5f12d18722" "q-110048/selection/7375110419d56f674ffdf8fc8c13e0a203f5131a6ebb34c02508c9f6e3dca36e" "q-110048/selection/1e1246969018f83ac88efee1a37d262b6f99142c4b4f712c8348e97e14a43105" "q-110048/selection/6413bed428971db3ca33a36b959ff6403755f399a59ccde28d247a491228db32" "q-110048/selection/b164d22226fc6e1c22c5fbf86a9eb47d04aed7cd22395189e7cdb0ed5538864c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110048" :question/id #uuid "372de79c-9c1e-56de-936b-79d5b2d31a54" :question/math-academy-id "q-110048" :question/problem "If $f(x)={sin}^{4}⁡({x}^{3}),$ find ${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$ as a function of ${f}^{-1}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y={sin}^{4}⁡({x}^{3}),$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx={sin}^{4}⁡({y}^{3})\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={f}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({sin}^{4}⁡({y}^{3})) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =4{sin}^{3}⁡({y}^{3})\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{3})\\cdot 3{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =12{y}^{2}{sin}^{3}⁡({y}^{3})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{12{y}^{2}{sin}^{3}⁡({y}^{3})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{3})} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{csc}^{3}⁡({y}^{3})\\operatorname{sec}⁡({y}^{3})}{12{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${f}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={f}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{f}^{-1}(x)] & =\\frac{{csc}^{3}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{3})\\operatorname{sec}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{3})}{12{[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{2}} \\\\ {({f}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{csc}^{3}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{3})\\operatorname{sec}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{3})}{12{[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-110048/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0196af83-9ef6-5bab-9f50-0aacf488f0cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110048"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
